checks_run.procedure:
Verify F-DG6-990 adversarially (sidecar code-security-reviewer.verifications.json):
- re-run the round-4 audit probe unedited on the real API;
- run an extended served-text probe;
- run mutant M1 (0130 removed) and the restore.

Line-level adversarial review of the repair diff (f56f1b3d..3c8b9a3 outside docs/delivery):
- migration 0130 against every trigger and guard of the five tables it writes (0028, 0069, 0074, 0097, 0101, 0117, 0127), the content hash and the instance pinning;
- the new scan and its exclusions;
- an upgrade probe over a demo-initialized 0129 database with administrator pre-states.

Search for any other served or rendered text that still names DG0-DG7:
- the string literals of every non-test product TypeScript file (apps/web, apps/worker, apps/api, packages/db/src including the demo dataset, packages/shared, packages/reporting), using the shipped scan() rule;
- the stored values of a demo-initialized database, fresh and upgraded, with no exclusions.

Targeted e2e on the real stack:
- A22, the Jobs screen, which renders the reworded job descriptions;
- A12, P6 scope isolation (search, deep link, evidence, exports, assistant, revocation);
- A17, failing connector to exception, with the synthetic webhook signing value.

